Show the subscription account a session's agent uses, left of the model picker.

The store keeps the account the runner reports (the omnigent.subscription label
on load, session.usage events after), and ComposerSubscription names it from
/v1/subscriptions/names. Tapping it explains what it means. A dot marks a
session that no longer uses the account Settings selects, with how to switch.
The tag shows nothing until the runner has reported an account and Settings
has an account for the provider.
The composer's right action group shrinks when it holds a control marked
data-composer-shrinkable, so a long account name truncates instead of pushing
the send button out of the composer; the new-chat composer is unchanged.
Applies after 0017-subscriptions.patch. Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).

